  "worked_solution": "The denominators are $5$ and $10.$ We can make a common denominator of $10.$\n\nWe split the shape on the right of the division sign into $2$ parts vertically:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/43424ef31fc44fa8485ee7a7b5a0ce6855858ad477d8365ac2ad898d25353f29.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{10}÷\\frac{6}{10}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n7÷6=1\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{10}÷\\frac{3}{5}=1\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
